> \[
> \boxed{\;k\in\{0,1,3\}\;}
> \]  
> for every integer \(n\ge3\).”

**Verification:**  
The three constructions demonstrate existence for \(k=0,1,3\).  The counting argument together with the (partially justified) classification of maximal‑capacity sunny lines shows that no other \(k\) can work.  Hence the final answer is correct.

